<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Gangani (Britain)</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of the Llŷn peninsula in north-west Wales, known from a headland Ptolemy named after them, with namesakes in western Ireland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Ptolemy's Geography</a> of about 150 names a Ganganorum Promontorium, the headland of the Gangani, on the coast of north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, generally identified with the tip of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llyn-peninsula">Llŷn</a> peninsula. Ptolemy does not list the Gangani among the inland peoples, so they may have been a small coastal group or a subdivision of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ordovices">Ordovices</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers or society. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llyn-peninsula">Llŷn</a> was a land of hillforts such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trer-ceiri">Tre'r Ceiri</a>, a stone-walled settlement occupied into the Roman period, and of farming and fishing communities. The identical name in Ireland, borne by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gangani-ireland">Gangani (Ireland)</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-shannon">Shannon</a>, has prompted theories of migration across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-sea">Irish Sea</a> in either direction.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Gangani are not mentioned again. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llyn-peninsula">Llŷn</a> later saw Irish settlement in the post-Roman period and became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-gwynedd">Kingdom of Gwynedd</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:61.69%;width:1.99%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Brittonic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>United Kingdom</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gangani</dd></dl></aside></div>

